<title>GERMANY: German resowings on 1997 grain area minimal - data.</title>
<headline>German resowings on 1997 grain area minimal - data.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Only small percentages of German 96/97 winter grain areas had to be replanted in the spring, data from the national statistics office showed.</p>
<p>It detailed the replanted areas as a percentage of the initial areas as follows -- winter wheat 1.1 percent, winter rye 0.6 percent, winter barley 2.5 percent and triticale 0.9 percent.</p>
<p>The figures showed the effect of winter damage was limited compared with the very harsh 95/96 winter.</p>
<p>The Bonn farm ministry last year said 1.2 percent of winter wheat, 1.5 percent of winter rye, 7.8 percent of winter barley and 1.8 percent of triticale were resown for the 1996 crop.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
